    summary """
        The whole suite ran at the feature commit. 756 of 757 passed on the first run; the one failure was no_tool_can_reach_the_sqlite_cache, which asserts every declared MCP tool has an output schema and which the seven knowledge.handoff_* tools fell off because output_schema was a hand-maintained match whose every arm returned the same shape. Deriving it from the TOOLS catalogue fixed it and removed that drift class; the test now passes. New coverage: crates/akr-cli/tests/advisor_packet.rs (nine cases, the load-bearing ones negative — a blind open leaks no worker note, the envelope does not narrow to what the worker examined, a fresh packet does not drift against itself) and an_advisor_packet_opens_the_same_way_from_either_surface in the MCP differential, which also proves opening over MCP does not stamp the packet.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

