record akr.evidence.d044-and-the-resolves-exemption-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "The corrected resolves exemption and the D-044 refusal pass, and the field migration is done"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:0dd6057aafb21ef86ae8d2bc7a659ed3c7fd1ebc
    command "cargo test -p akr-core --test v_rules && cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness && cargo test -p akr-cli --test writes"
    summary """
        v_rules 86 passed 0 failed, freshness 42 passed 0 failed, writes 35 passed 0 failed.

        The resolves exemption was wrong in its first form and the review caught it. Resolving a
        question creates a revision: /2 becomes resolved and /1 becomes superseded, so a pin at the
        revision that was open when the answer was written lands on the superseded one and was
        still refused — with the help telling the author to use a historical relation and pin it,
        which is what they had done. Exempting Resolved alone passed every test and would have
        failed every user, because akr revise auto-repoints live pins: resolves [@q/1] is rewritten
        to /2 before check ever sees it, so a record built through the CLI never reaches the state
        the bug lives in. v006_passes_for_resolves_pinned_at_the_revision_that_was_open builds the
        ledger directly for that reason and is the test the first version should have had.

        D-044 refuses an unversioned supersedes. v006_refuses_an_unversioned_supersedes pins three
        cases: the unversioned cross-key form is AKR-L021, the pinned form at a retired target is
        clean, and the same-key revision chain is untouched because head() computes that and it is
        not a cross-key claim.

        Field migration complete in the three ledgers this session maintained. Lege-ecosystem's
        decision.jbig2-is-the-default-pdf-text-format-again carried the unversioned form and is now
        pinned to /1, the revision it replaced. LegeOS's was removed earlier in the same pass for a
        different reason. All three report no diagnostics under check --views-current.
        """
}

