record akr.evidence.papercut-retest-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "Ten reported AKR defects re-tested on 2026-09-08; seven are fixed and three were never defects"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:0dd6057aafb21ef86ae8d2bc7a659ed3c7fd1ebc
    command "re-ran each reported reproduction against akr 0.5.0, in the reporting workspace or in a throwaway one"
    summary """
        ALREADY FIXED, each re-run rather than assumed.
        The descendant-commit gate versus a bulk historical port: waived for a legacy-sourced record
        by D-028, extended to ordinary committed completions by D-029; akr explain AKR-R022 states
        the waiver and bpg-rs checks clean at HEAD with its whole ledger committed.
        akr validate exists as an alias of check, closing two papercuts that said the CLI had no
        validate subcommand.
        akr get shows a work record's acceptance check ids at default detail, closing the papercut
        that said complete had to fail once to reveal them.
        akr revise --from is a slot overlay and keeps unmentioned slots: proposed a record with
        scope, intent and note, revised supplying only intent, and both survived in the record file.
        akr evidence add followed by akr complete needs no build between them: done five times in
        one pass in the Lege-ecosystem ledger and twice more here.
        Concurrent writes no longer lose records: six akr evidence add processes started together
        against one fresh workspace, all six reported success, all six records present,
        .akr/cache/write.lock created. Under the reported behaviour two of six would have survived.
        The 0.1.0 stub renderers are gone; all seven views exist and emit.

        NOT DEFECTS.
        akr get --format json completed in 0.8s here and 1.5s in Lege-ecosystem, against a 14-second
        report from bpg-rs. Not reproducible; workspace-specific or already fixed.
        topic on a work record raises AKR-T034 "topic applies only to normative kinds" and aborts
        with nothing written. The message names the rule and the fix; this is the validator working.
        Freshness rebuilds hanging for minutes: misattributed. Roughly a hundred akr invocations
        across four workspaces on 2026-09-08, the largest LegeOS at 691 revisions, all returned in
        1 to 2 seconds. The original report came from that same LegeOS workspace on the machine that
        later locked for 45 minutes with one process at 19.9 GB RSS and swap exhausted; see
        legeos.observation.one-developer-tool-froze-the-machine-for-45-minutes-20260908. Same tool,
        same workspace, same ledger sizes, and the only variable was memory pressure. The report
        predates the diagnosis.

        STILL LIVE, re-confirmed and sharpened rather than closed: akr context refuses both a
        decision (AKR-X003) and a completed work record (AKR-X002), so there is no orientation
        target for finished work or for the decisions governing it.
        """
}

