record akr.evidence.relation-fixes-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "The relation fixes pass, and the new check found two contradictory live decisions in the field"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:0dd6057aafb21ef86ae8d2bc7a659ed3c7fd1ebc
    command "cargo test -p akr-core --test v_rules && cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness && cargo test -p akr-cli --test writes"
    summary """
        Suites: v_rules 84 passed 0 failed, freshness 42 passed 0 failed, writes 35 passed 0 failed.

        Two new v_rules cases.
        v006_passes_for_resolves_pointing_at_the_question_it_resolved pins the exemption: a resolved
        question is the expected end state of resolving it, so the answering record may name it.
        v006_reports_a_supersedes_edge_that_has_not_superseded_anything pins all three directions —
        the unversioned form fires, the pinned form fires identically, and once the target really is
        retired the edge is telling the truth and says nothing.

        The pinned case is there because a throwaway workspace showed the reported defect was not
        what it looked like. One observation superseded by a successor naming it without a revision,
        one with: both targets stayed verified, akr why-current resolved both as LIVE, akr check
        said nothing about either. A cross-key supersedes edge never retires its target in either
        form, so a fix framed as naming the missing revision suffix would have told authors to write
        something that changes nothing.

        Run against the three ledgers this session maintained, the new check immediately found two
        real defects that every previous check had reported clean.
        In Lege-ecosystem, decision.jbig2-is-the-default-pdf-text-format-again had declared
        supersedes on decision.truetyping-is-the-default-pdf-text-format since it was written, and
        both were live: two contradictory decisions about which format is the default, both rendered
        into CURRENT-STATE.md. Retiring the old one tripped AKR-R021 on work.glyph-font-text-output's
        implements edge, which was repointed to the successor first.
        In LegeOS, decision.agplv3-own-code carried an unversioned supersedes on
        decision.toolchain-licence-namespace. Written when the target was at an earlier revision, it
        means "the current head" under D-009, so it re-aimed as the target gained revisions and by
        2026-09-08 named revision 3, which is active. The edge was not merely inert; it had become a
        moving target, asserting that one live decision had replaced another while neither had moved.

        All three ledgers report no diagnostics after the repairs.
        """
}

