record akr.evidence.six-point-of-failure-fixes-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "Six fixes verified on real workspaces, not only in tests"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:0dd6057aafb21ef86ae8d2bc7a659ed3c7fd1ebc
    command "cargo check -p akr-core -p akr-cli && cargo test -p akr-core --test freshness && cargo test -p akr-cli --test writes"
    summary """
        Suites: freshness 42 passed 0 failed, writes 35 passed 0 failed, both crates check clean.

        Each fix was then exercised through the built binary against a real workspace rather than a
        fixture.

        A directory scope matches what is under it. A new case covers tools/, tools, tools/**,
        tools/* and tools/build.py all matching one tracked file, with toolsmiths/ still reporting
        AKR-G023 so the fix cannot swallow a genuinely absent directory. Before this, an author who
        wrote path "tools/" was told the path had moved or been deleted about a directory holding
        twenty-five tracked files.

        An MCP tool name is recognised as one. akr knowledge.context answers "is an MCP tool name,
        not a CLI command; the CLI equivalent is akr context (AGENTS.md has the whole mapping)";
        akr knowledge_evidence_add maps to akr evidence add; akr knowledge.validate maps to akr
        check. The edit-distance suggestion still handles an ordinary typo.

        The workspace one level down is named. Run from the shared parent that holds this run's
        fifteen checkouts, AKR-C011 now reads "no workspace here, but 15 in subdirectories: AKR,
        Evidence-intake-project, Kitchen-Concept, Lege-ecosystem, LegeOS, SaveYourSkin,
        Thai-alphabet-app, agent-pack, and 7 more — run akr from one of them, or pass --dir",
        instead of suggesting akr init in a directory that is not a git repository.

        The gitignore reconciliation reports. Run against LegeOS, whose workspace predates the
        .agent/handoffs/ entry: ".gitignore is missing 1 entry(ies) akr init now writes:
        .agent/handoffs/ — add them, or these paths accumulate untracked". LegeOS is carrying 49
        untracked packets for exactly this reason.

        The same LegeOS run also demonstrates the completed-record change on a real ledger:
        AKR-G023 on legeos.work.home-file-surface/2 for scope path "docs/homefield.md", a
        completed record whose scope names a file that no longer exists. That warning did not
        appear before today.

        A propose or revise naming a commit the repository lacks is refused at the write, by the
        same ensure_commits_exist that akr evidence add has used since 0.4.

        A complete on a record with no acceptance block now says so: "completed with no acceptance
        checks; nothing was verified".
        """
}

